This is the C++ code
```c++
class CcdImageList {
public:
    CcdImageList() {
        this->m_images = new CcdImage*();
    }

    void addImage(CcdImage* img) {
        m_images->insert(img->id);
    }

    const char* getUniqueName() const {
        return "images/" + std::to_string(m_images.size() - 1);
    }
};
```

When calling this in python with SWIG, the following code works:

```python
image_list = CcdImageList()
image_list.addImage(Image1)
image_list.addImage(Image2)

for i in image_list:
    print(i.getUniqueName())
```

This works because the `list` is converted to a Python list and can be iterated over.

